{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-degree-two-baryon-weight","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:degree-two-baryon-weight","kind":"proposition","title":"Degree-2 weight $\\beta_2 = -2[3]_q$ from baryon quantum number","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-wedderburn-mass-formula"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta2_approx","text":"degree-two-baryon-weight.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:degree-two-baryon-weight\"></a><p><em>The coefficient of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_2</code> in the Wedderburn mass formula is</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\beta_2 = -2[3]_q\n          = -2 \\cdot \\frac{q^3 - q^{-3}}{q - q^{-1}}\n          \\approx -6.087</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[3]_q</code> is the quantum 3-integer.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.17.15"}
